[{"id":34224,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34224\">#1</a> Prompted by <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2/topic/internal.20set/near/34223\">discussion</a> in the thread on “<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/internal%20sets\">internal sets</a>” (badly named so) I have added to <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set\">h-set</a></em> a comment in <em><a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set#RelationToInternalSets\">Properties - Relation to internal set</a></em>.</p>","timestamp":1347524915,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":34226,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34226\">#2</a> I have also edited and expanded the <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set#Idea\">Idea section</a> a little. Please check if you can live with this.</p>","timestamp":1347525563,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":34278,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34278\">#3</a> I also disagree with this, for the same reason I mentioned in the other thread.  Usually, in homotopy type theory (especially when regarded as the internal language of an <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-topos) it <em>is</em> the 0-truncated objects which play the role of “sets”.</p>","timestamp":1347574459,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":34336,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34336\">#4</a> What shall we do? </p>\n<p>I suppose we need to more thoroughly keep qualifiers around. Are we on the safe side with the “n-strictness”-terminology?</p>\n<p>Right now I can’t check or do anything, as I have a connection of about one bit per second. But I’ll try to fix later whatever mess I may have created.</p>","timestamp":1347639405,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":34582,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34582\">#5</a> I’ve rewritten the section “Relation to internal sets” at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set\">h-set</a> from the perspectitve I advocated in the <a href=\"#narrow/channel/2/topic/internal.20set/near/34284\">other thread</a>.  I don’t have time right now to hash out the right “strict” qualifiers, unfortunately.  Can you live with what I wrote for now?</p>","timestamp":1348180529,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":34584,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/34584\">#6</a> Thanks! Very nice and very helpful.</p>","timestamp":1348181176,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":65258,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/h-set/near/65258\">#7</a> At <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set\">h-set</a></em> there was no mentioning that they form a pretopos. I have added a minimum <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/h-set#PretoposOfHsets\">here</a>.</p>","timestamp":1509089094,"subject":"h-set","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]